#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define the gate {#1-define-the-gate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The gate is a "
"[`BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp) "
"holding a twirled layer of six disjoint `CZ` gates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Set up local simulation {#2-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Pauli indices inside each map are local to the gate, in ascending "
"physical-qubit order:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Define the noise with a correlated `ZZ` term and a weaker `XX` term on each "
"`CZ` pair, plus a single-qubit `Z` term everywhere; measurement gets a bit-"
"flip term per qubit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build a box for measurement to learn.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each entry of `layer_noise_model` pairs one of those boxes with the map to "
"apply to it. Use the stabilizer simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` "
"to make the simulated data reproducible.\n"
msgstr ""

